<title>FRANCE: LVMH up on Guinness/Grand Met merger.</title>
<headline>LVMH up on Guinness/Grand Met merger.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French drinks and luxury goods group LVMH climbed 2.32 percent to 1,410 francs, on volume of 37,929 shares, at 0920 GMT, with traders citing the planned merger between Guinness Plc and Grand Metropolitan Plc .</p>
<p>&quot;We like it (the merger) for earnings enhancement for LVMH,&quot; said an equity salesman at a big French brokerage.</p>
<p>Despite opposition by LVMH Chairman Bernard Arnault to the merger, the 14 percent stake in Guinness held by the French firm will be revalued by the deal, which should boost stocks in the retail sector which have been stable in recent years, he added.</p>
</text>
